  "snippet": "#​496 — November 6, 2026 Read on the Web React Status Discord Dropping Electron and React Native for a Rust Rewrite — Discord, one of React Native's best-known users, is moving away, with its CTO 𝕏 showing off a Rust des...",
  "coverImage": "https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ouvobggjw2zmigv3z8xx.jpg",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"padding-left: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p>#​496 — November 6, 2026</p></td>\n<td align=\"right\" style=\"padding-right: 4px; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"><p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192600/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the Web</a></p></td>\n</tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #333;\">\n<div style=\"font-size: 2.7em; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.3em; margin-bottom: 0px;\"> React Status</div>\n</div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192557/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/ouvobggjw2zmigv3z8xx.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192557/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.1em; line-height: 1.4em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.theverge.com\">Discord Dropping Electron <em>and</em> React Native for a Rust Rewrite</a></span> — Discord, one of React Native's best-known users, is moving away, with its CTO 𝕏 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192558/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">showing off a Rust desktop client</a> built on GPUI using 290MB of RAM, with mobile keeping native UI over Rust code shared with the desktop client.</p>\n<p>Tom Warren (The Verge) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>▶️ Just prior to this reveal, Software Mansion interviewed Discord's Chas Jhin about how React Native development works at Discord's scale, in the ominously titled <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192559/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">'Maybe React Native Is Impossible'</a>.</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192556/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"130\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/01c20d97.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"130\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192556/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"master.dev\">Run AI Coding Models on Your Own Machine</a></span> — Local models are now good enough for everyday coding. Learn to run them on your own Mac or GPU, wire them into your editor and terminal agents, and keep your code private with no per-token bill.</p>\n<p>Master.dev <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192560/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">A Roadmap for Redux Toolkit v2.x and 3.0</a></span> — Mark Erikson has laid out the roadmap for Redux (complete with a neat history lesson) with RTK 3.0 expected in six to eight months, going ESM-only with 'React 19-scale' breaking changes. But a run of 2.x releases will ship the groundwork first, starting with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192561/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">2.14</a> this week.</p>\n<p>Mark Erikson </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><strong>IN BRIEF:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ Update to Next.js 16.4.5 or 15.5.29, as appropriate: <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192562/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">the November security release</a> fixes seven advisories. Most are Cache Components bugs, so the post is worth reading.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🤖 TanStack Query maintainer Dominik Dorfmeister says <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192563/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">work on Query v6 can start once 'slop PRs' stop coming in</a> and taking up his time, leading to a thread on the effects of AI-made contributions on maintainers.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Vercel is <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192564/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">folding Next.js's Data Cache into Runtime Cache</a> with bigger allocations but… new per-read and per-write pricing. Hobby teams migrate on November 29, but <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192565/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">check the dates and prices</a> for your use case.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Vercel builds also now <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192566/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">block known-malicious npm package versions</a> before and during install, on all plans and with no configuration needed.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192567/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Next.js is Prototyping Go(lang) Route Handlers</a></span> — A merged experimental PR lets an App Router route be a <code>route.go</code> file exporting <code>GET</code> and friends, compiled by Turbopack and run in supervised Go-powered workers. Tim says Rust could follow along the same path.</p>\n<p>Tim Neutkens (Vercel) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192568/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.alexandretrotel.org\">Understanding React Internals: A Deep Dive</a></span> — A seven-part, source-grounded tour of React's internals that, unusually, starts from the server end before getting to fibers, lanes and the commit phase.</p>\n<p>Alexandre Trotel </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192569/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"developer.amazon.com\">Amazon's React Native-Based <em>Vega</em> OS Hits 2.0</a></span> — Vega, the React Native-based OS behind newer Fire TV devices, is out of beta. SDK 2.0 takes apps from RN 0.72 to 0.83, bringing the React Compiler and Hermes v1 into play. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192570/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">The release notes</a> go into more detail than the post.</p>\n<p>Barak Schlosser (Amazon) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192571/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Why We Finally Left Next.js for TanStack Start</a> – Production memory leaks in two Next.js 16.3 releases were the last straw. <cite>Harrison Milbradt</cite></p>\n<p>📄 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192572/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Writable Derived State: Stop Synchronizing State</a> – Using <code>clientData ?? serverData</code> instead of a <code>useEffect</code> that wipes user edits on refetch. <cite>Corbin Crutchley</cite></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>🛠  Code, Tools &amp; Libraries</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192574/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/bl5l2bsrtakodwasfc7d.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192574/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">Skullet: Skeleton Loading States Measured from Your Components</a></span> — Hand it sample data and it renders your real component invisibly, measures everything, and draws a matching skeleton to reduce layout shifts when data arrives. The <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192575/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">docs</a> have a neat <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192576/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">How it Works</a> section explaining the technique.</p>\n<p>Lochie Axon </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192577/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"v3.parceljs.org\">Parcel 3 Alpha: A Rust Rewrite with React Compiler, Tailwind and RSC</a></span> — Parcel's core is now a Rust binary with no Node dependency, and the team reports cold builds up to 100x faster than v2. React Compiler (opt-in), Tailwind and MDX are built in, with RSC support in beta.</p>\n<p>Devon Govett (Parcel) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><span>🤖</span> <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192578/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">Reticle: Let Coding Agents Verify Their Changes Against Your Running App</a></span> — A dev-only SDK and MCP server so coding agents can drive your running app, inspect network requests, application state, and console activity, and return a pass, fail or 'can't tell' verdict with what needs fixing.</p>\n<p>Reticle Labs </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192579/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/pqjgb8mjxtsjhmrzjeis.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192580/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-size: 1.05em;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"github.com\">react-resizable-panels Gets a VS Code-Style <code>Workspace</code> Component</a></span> — Brian Vaughn's popular panel library now does dockable tabs you can drag to split or merge panes, and moved tabs keep their state rather than remounting. There's <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192579/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584;\" target=\"_blank\">a live demo here</a>.</p>\n<p>Brian Vaughn </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192581/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Preact 11.2</a> – Now has a <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192582/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">runtime for React Compiler output</a> via <code>preact/compat</code>, plus scoped custom element registries in shadow roots.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192583/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">XState 6.0 Beta</a> – <em>\"No further breaking changes are planned\"</em> for public APIs, and <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192584/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>@xstate/react</code> 7</a> is in beta alongside.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192585/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">TanStack Redact 0.3</a> – The lightweight, synchronous-only React / React DOM replacement adds browser SPA plugins for Webpack and Rspack.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192586/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React Native 0.89 RC</a> – Faster text layout and native module calls, legacy bridge APIs gone. Stable expected in December.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192587/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Storybook 11.0 Beta</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>📰 Classifieds</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>🤖 <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192588/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Fimo</a> gives your marketers a visual editor and AI agents for SEO and GEO. No more tickets for your React devs. By the Strapi team.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192589/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">QVAC</a> allows you to run any AI capabilities for free, on your phone or laptop, privately. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192589/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Try the QVAC SDK now on GitHub</a>.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0;\"><p>📢  Elsewhere in the ecosystem</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>James Long <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192590/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">has been reviving <em>Prepack</em></a>, Facebook's abandoned JavaScript partial evaluator. There's a <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192591/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">React demo</a> where a pretend site is server rendered three ways, by React, by Prepack's output (which essentially 'compiles' React away), and a hybrid, with the render times to compare.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192592/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Node.js 27 <em>Alpha</em></a> has landed, the first version using Node's new <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192593/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">release process</a> (where a release will spend six months in 'alpha' before going <em>Current</em>), while <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192594/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Node 26</a> is now the new LTS line.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Chrome 157 rolled out this week with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192595/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">HTML-in-Canvas now stable</a>. It provides a way to draw real DOM elements into 2D, WebGL and WebGPU canvases. <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192596/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">The demos</a> are striking.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Vercel has released <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192597/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Geist Serif</a>, a new serif font that shares metrics with <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192598/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Geist Sans</a> so the two can mix cleanly. It's not on Google Fonts yet, but the <a href=\"https://react.statuscode.com/link/192599/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #3c2584; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\"><code>geist</code> npm package</a> includes it.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
  "attachments": []
}